RF.put("questb:b35",{"8595":{"id":8595,"t":"Mortal Champions","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Qiraji Lord's Insignia The Prophet Skeram in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Emperor Vek'lor in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more","back":"Killing one Qiraji lord is a notable accomplishment for a mortal, ‹name›. They are however, numerous and powerful. Continue to defeat them to prove your worth as our champion.","done":"You continue to serve us well, ‹name›. Our pact remains in place.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Raid Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8595\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 9,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions this quest\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n3,300 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8515":{"id":8515,"t":"The Alliance Needs Thick Leather!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 44.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Leather to Marta Finespindle at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"Oh boy, this is going to be great! ‹class›, the Ahn'Qiraj war effort is in full swing, and I've been put in charge of keeping track of all of the thick leather that comes in. We'll make tons of things with it, but first we need to get a ton of it. And I mean that literally! That's where you come in.\nSo, do you think you can go out there and bring me back a nice, fat stack of thick leather? Do yah, do yah?!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Is that the thick leather you have there in your pack, ‹class›? Is it? I can't wait for you to hand it over! Everyone is going to be so pleased with us don't you think?","done":"Oh, I knew you could do it, ‹class›, I just knew it! I'll get these into the right hands as soon as I can. Now, let's see here. Hmm, looks like our tally is coming along rather nicely. You should check back with me in just a moment once I'm done counting to see if we need more. Cuz if we do, you're the one I want out there gathering it up for me!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.6,"y":33.3,"n":"Marta Finespindle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8115":{"id":8115,"t":"Control Five Bases","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Control 5 bases in Arathi Basin at the same time, then return to Field Marshal Oslight at Refuge Pointe.","desc":"‹name›, battling for the resources of Arathi Basin is a bloody undertaking. Your services to the League of Arathor are as needed as they are appreciated.\nAnd we have one more task for you.\nThe League wishes to make one strong push against the Defilers' occupation of Arathi Basin. We want them driven out of every strategic point on the battlefield!\nIt will not be easy, but if anyone can get it done, it is you.","rew":"You will receive:\nArathor Battle Tabard\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with The League of Arathor","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":45.8,"y":45.5,"n":"Field Marshal Oslight","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"675":{"id":675,"t":"Raising Spirits","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tor'gan.","desc":"<Gor'mul tosses the amulet into the ground.>\nTor'gan sent you, didn't he? Pah! Why he feels some mercy towards me I would not understand. Mercy was denied me when I was not allowed to die with my Warchief in battle. A cruel blow fate has dealt me...","rew":"Experience: 270\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"It did not work, I see. Nonetheless, I feel that showing him the power of the shamans will eventually return Gor'mul to his once proud self. The amulet's power was not great enough to show him our newfound power.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":72.6,"y":33.9,"n":"Gor'mul","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":74.7,"y":36.3,"n":"Tor'gan","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"8995":{"id":8995,"t":"Mea Culpa, Lord Valthalak","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon Lord Valthalak. Dispatch him, and use Lord Valthalak's Amulet on the corpse. Then, return Lord Valthalak's Amulet to the Spirit of Lord Valthalak.\nLord Valthalak's Amulet\nLord Valthalak slain\nProvided: Brazier of Beckoning","desc":"All is now ready, ‹name›.\nWhen alive, Lord Valthalak used to inhabit what is now The Beast's chamber. Go there and use the Brazier of Beckoning to summon forth Lord Valthalak. It will reincorporate him, so he'll have to be killed again. I'd take care of The Beast first, and be sure take enough friends along to survive the upper portion of Blackrock Spire.\nOnce you've dispatched Valthalak, use the amulet on his corpse. With his spirit reunified, he'll likely want his amulet back, as well.\nGood luck!","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"‹class›, you dare disturb my rest!","done":"How fortunate for you that I know you're not part of the original group that stole this from me.\nI'll take back what is mine now, mortal! Give the amulet to me!","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2755":{"id":2755,"t":"Joys of Omosh","lv":36,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Watch and learn the Omosh Dance of Joy.","desc":"Orokk is not crying, ‹name›. Soot is in eye.\n<Orokk wipes a tear away.>\nThere is one last Omosh family secret Orokk will teach you. Orokk will die happy, thanks to ‹name›.\nLearn Omosh dance of joy and then you learn fist of iron!","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Barbaric Iron Gloves\nExperience: 280","done":"<Orokk pants.>\nIt has been a very long time since Orokk has done the Omosh dance of joy. Learn now, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.2,"y":22.4,"n":"Orokk Omosh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97955":{"id":97955,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Nurse Neela in Brill to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","back":"I can teach you once you've gained some skill with your profession.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.2,"y":55.4,"n":"Eleanor Shackleton","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.8,"y":52.8,"n":"Nurse Neela","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94275":{"id":94275,"t":"Craftsmans writ solid sharpening stone","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Solid Sharpening Stone\nSolid Sharpening Stone","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Solid Sharpening Stone, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Solid Sharpening Stone Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94275","cats":["crafting"]},"94355":{"id":94355,"t":"Craftsmans writ tuxedo jacket","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Tuxedo Jacket\nTuxedo Jacket","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Tuxedo Jacket, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Tuxedo Jacket Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94355","cats":["crafting"]},"995":{"id":995,"t":"Escape Through Stealth","lv":20,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escape the Furbolg cave and meet Terenthis in Auberdine.","desc":"All right then... if you're sure, we'll sneak out of here. Let us leave when you're ready.\nRemember, after you've escaped, meet Terenthis back in Auberdine. I'll head there on my own since I'll probably be moving faster than you.","rew":"You will receive:\nScarab Trousers\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 775\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Yes, ‹name›?","done":"‹name›! I'm pleased to see you've returned successfully. Your assistance to Volcor has given me faith that we can overcome the challenges facing us here in Darkshore and beyond.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":45,"y":85.3,"n":"Volcor","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":39.4,"y":43.5,"n":"Terenthis","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"92755":{"id":92755,"t":"Mysterious mysticism","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 3 Greater Mystic Essences to Halea in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nGreater Mystic Essence x 3\nGelkis Clan Centaur:","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFormula: Enchant Bracer - Lesser Agility Formula: Enchant Bracer - Lesser Healing Power\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+1,000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nLevel 35 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 31 33 38 44 Side Both factions Quest ID 92755","cats":["desolace"]},"835":{"id":835,"t":"Securing the Lines","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Dustwind Savages and 8 Dustwind Storm Witches for Rezlak near Drygulch Ravine.\nDustwind Savage slain : 0/ 12\nDustwind Storm Witch slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Gazlowe told me once, \"Rezlak. There's one thing you need to know in life, and that's if you want something done well, do it yourself.\"\nI can't deal with losing all our caravans, so I'm just going to take matters into my own hands. Drygulch Ravine lies through the eastern part of Razorwind Canyon. If we kill all the harpies there, the routes will be safe.\nOf course, there was one other thing that Gazlowe taught me, and that's \"You can get anything done for a price.\" So, going to help me out, ‹name›?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHarpy Wing Clipper Hickory Shortbow Blemished Wooden Staff\nExperience: 875\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"You wouldn't think it from a guy like my boss Gazlowe, but he always seemed to know the score. \"Don't be afraid to take that big step\", he said.\nHarpies won't stop bothering us and the caravans won't stop being attacked unless we do something about it, eh?","done":"I think I can breathe easy now, knowing that the harpies won't be bothering our supply caravans anymore. And not one moment too soon, either. I hear I'm being sent some fun little toys with the next shipment!\nYou're pretty good at what you do, ‹name›, you ought to track down my boss in Ratchet. I'll bet he could find some work for you.\nOh, and don't worry, I wouldn't forget to pay you for the service you provided me.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":46.4,"y":22.9,"n":"Rezlak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1395":{"id":1395,"t":"Supplies for Nethergarde","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Crate of Powerstones to Quartermaster Lungertz, before the powerstones expire.\nCrate of Power Stones\nProvided: Crate of Power Stones","desc":"This crate of powerstones needs to go to Nethergarde Keep, in the Blasted Lands. They won't hold their power for long, so we can't ship them with the next caravan.\nYou must take them, and you must take them quickly.\nBring them to Quartermaster Lungertz in Nethergarde Keep. To reach the keep, you must travel east through Deadwind Pass, then east through the Swamp of Sorrows, then south through the Blasted Lands.\nUse caution, ‹name›. You will travel through dangerous lands, yet you must not fail.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 50 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,900\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello! Don't mind all the commotion, it's just business as usual at Nethergarde Keep.\nYou have something for me?","done":"Ah, the powerstones! The mages will be happy to see these!\nMany thanks, ‹name›. I know your trip from Darkshire was not an easy one.\nDuskwood Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":46.2,"n":"Watchmaster Sorigal","s":1},{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":66.5,"y":21.4,"n":"Quartermaster Lungertz","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"35":{"id":35,"t":"Further Concerns","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Marshal Dughan wants you to speak with Guard Thomas.","desc":"If you are concerned that the rumors of murlocs are true, then do this -- travel to the eastern Elwynn bridge and speak with Guard Thomas. He has been stationed at the bridge for the past week and will know the state of the area.\nBring me his report.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Yes, murlocs have settled in and around the streams of eastern Elwynn. We don't know why they are here, but they are aggressive and at least semi-intelligent.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":74,"y":72.2,"n":"Guard Thomas","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"3635":{"id":3635,"t":"Gnome Engineering","lv":47,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"If you wish to learn more about Gnome Engineering, take the Manual of Engineering Disciplines to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay.\nManual of Engineering Disciplines\nProvided: Manual of Engineering Disciplines","desc":"Engineering at the expert level breaks into two disciplines: gnome and goblin. While I think it is a waste, you should be aware of gnome specialization. They make items and gadgets that claim to change the world, but rarely work.\n‹name›, read this manual. If you wish to learn how to make metal paper weights, then take the manual to Oglethorpe Obnoticus in Booty Bay. Remember - membership is permanent and prevents joining the other discipline, so make sure you are sure before finishing his task.","rew":"Experience: 420","back":"Hello there! If you've come about a homing robot that may have smashed through a wall of your domicile, then I will refer you to my barrister in advance. Otherwise, what can I do for you today?","done":"You've come to learn about gnome engineering, eh? Well, you've come to the right gnome. While the ruling faction of Gnomeregan may use politics to ostracize those they view as an intellectual threat, they know that knowledge is something they cannot control.\nThey and I both know that when I left Gnomeregan, they lost one of their greatest gnome engineers alive today. If you're a capable student, I'll teach you what I know.\nUndercity Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":75.3,"y":73.1,"n":"Graham Van Talen","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.4,"y":76.4,"n":"Oglethorpe Obnoticus","e":1}],"cats":["engineering"]},"95795":{"id":95795,"t":"Fallen in the fen","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Dorin Songblade.","desc":"<You cover the dwarf's body with his cloak.>\nTravel to Lakeshire and personally inform Dorin Songblade what became of his brother within the Excavation Sites.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDaewyn's Girdle Songblade Stabilizer\nExperience: 6,150","done":"Ah no...\n<He buries his head in his hands and sobs.>\nI should 'ave gone with 'em.\nMuch of what I was smithin' was for 'im, was plannin' a surprise but it wasn't ready when he came by gettin' things for his journey.\nNow that these are finished, I don't have it in me to reforge or sell any of it.\nYou can have this. It's the least I can do for you, bringing me this grim day.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":30.8,"y":46.6,"n":"Dorin Songblade","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"5155":{"id":5155,"t":"Forces of Jaedenar","lv":51,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Enter Jaedenar and slay 4 Jaedenar Hounds, 4 Jaedenar Guardsmen, 6 Jaedenar Adepts, and 6 Jaedenar Cultists before returning to Greta Mosshoof in Felwood.\nJaedenar Hound slain : 0/ 4\nJaedenar Guardian slain : 0/ 4\nJaedenar Adept slain : 0/ 6\nJaedenar Cultist slain : 0/ 6","desc":"If I am to trust you in this matter, you will first have to prove yourself.\nI must know that you are an enemy of the Shadow Council--the ones responsible for many evils here and abroad.\nTravel deeper into Felwood. To the west you will see a path leading to Jaedenar. It is there that the Council plots with the Burning Legion.\nEnter the depths of one of the corrupted Barrow Dens they inhabit and slay their kind. Return to me after you've done this. Then I will know you truly seek to help us.","rew":"Experience: 4,900","back":"How goes your fight, ‹name›? I know the shedding of blood as proof of honor can be disgusting to some, but you must understand that it serves two goals: you make my task easier by hurting their numbers, and we gain a respect for each other that will only make us stronger in times to come.\nI hope you understand.","done":"Good, ‹name›! With their numbers weakening, we can further press them.\nHow was your first taste of their power? Were they as strong as you thought they would be? Stronger? Or perhaps they were no challenge for you at all. Wouldn't that be something?\nWe can discuss the details of your exploits later. There are other things we must focus on now.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.2,"y":82.1,"n":"Greta Mosshoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4115":{"id":4115,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50,"y":80,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"515":{"id":515,"t":"Elixir of Agony","lv":30,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Glistening Stompers.","obj":"Bring the Mudsnout Mixture, a Strong Troll's Blood Potion, 5 Daggerspine Scales and 5 Torn Fin Eyes to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\nLesser Troll's Blood Elixir\n5 Daggerspine Scale\n5 Torn Fin Eye\nProvided: Mudsnout Mixture","desc":"A mudsnout composite? Absolutely brilliant! Why didn't I think of that?\nLet me contribute my colloid of decay to this devilish brew.\nIn order to activate the contaminating agents in this mudsnout mixture, Lydon is going to need a strong troll's blood potion, as well as some daggerspine scales and torn fin eyes from the southern coast of Hillsbrad. He'll know what to do once you've gathered him all the reagents. And my, how anxious I am to hear how his experiment goes!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHigh Apothecary Cloak Meditative Sash Glistening Stompers\nNew in Forever: Glistening Stompers.\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"So glad to see you back, ‹name›. I was growing so terribly bored here. Not a single entertaining thing to do besides poison and disease Umpi and reanimate her. . .over and over and over again.\nHow went the trip to the Undercity? Were you fortunate enough to slaughter any humans along the way?","done":"The excitement of this experiment has me feeling giddy! You have been such a great help, ‹name›. Together we will spread death and disease to this land!\nUndercity Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":48.8,"y":69.3,"n":"Master Apothecary Faranell","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"7635":{"id":7635,"t":"A Proper String","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Stoma the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Black Dragon Sinew. Should you find this sinew, return it to Stoma in Felwood.\nMature Black Dragon Sinew Onyxia 40 %","desc":"Vartrus may offer you the stave to create a bow of Ancients but only I can enchant the string required to complete the bow.\nIt is a simple task, puny one. Slay a mature black dragon and remove the sinew from its bones. Return that sinew to me and I shall enchant the material into an almost indestructible bow string.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted Black Dragon Sinew\nExperience: 9,950","back":"I am certain that you will have little difficulty in finding and slaying a black dragon, ‹name›. Do not waste my time with idle chatter.","done":"A most foul dragon this one was. The sinew reeks of evil.\nGive me a moment to cleanse the filth from this flesh and apply the proper enchantments.\nStart Stoma the Ancient End Stoma the Ancient Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable No Quest ID 7635\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 19,900 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Ancient Leaf\nFind the owner of the Ancient Petrified Leaf.\nAncient Petrified Leaf\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] A Proper String this quest\nStoma the Ancient has asked that you bring him a Mature Black Dragon Sinew.\nStoma the Ancient\n9,950 XP","cats":["hunter"]},"8275":{"id":8275,"t":"Taking Back Silithus","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.","desc":"Attention, heroes of the Alliance! The silithid menace has been left unchecked for too long. Unfettered by any real opposition, they've been preparing all this time for a large-scale expansion.\nCenarion Circle forces are gathering in Silithus to take the fight to these wretched creatures and all able-bodied adventurers are hereby called to join us!\nDon't wait until it's too late! Aid us in the defense of Azeroth! Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold for specific instructions!","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+10 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"Excellent, a new recruit answering the call to arms against the silithid. Welcome to Cenarion Hold, ‹class›. I am pleased to see the words of our emissaries are reaching heroes of your caliber. You will find no shortage of opportunities to help us in our efforts here and I expect you'll quickly prove to be a valuable ally to our cause.\nDun Morogh Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.5,"y":28.7,"n":"Cenarion Emissary Jademoon","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8675":{"id":8675,"t":"Skychaser the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"Your spirit burns with life, young ‹class›. I accept the homage you pay, and offer in return this token...","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.7,"y":47.1,"n":"Elder Skychaser","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1955":{"id":1955,"t":"The Exorcism","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill the Demon of the Orb, then speak with Tabetha.\nDemon of the Orb slain","desc":"Now that we have a summoner's orb, we must exorcise the demon within it. I can do that. That's the easy part.\nYou're the one who has the hard job. You're the one who has to kill the demon once it's out.\nAnd you'll have to be quick. If you take too long then he'll jump back in the orb and we'll have to start over!\nSo get yourself ready. Prepare your strongest spells and keep your potions handy, and go get a friend if you have one. Because this isn't going to be pretty.","rew":"Experience: 2,350","back":"You'll have to kill that demon to remove its taint from the orb, ‹name›.","done":"Nicely done, ‹name›! You gave that demon a lesson he won't soon forget.\nHe'll think twice before he sticks his ugly head back in this world, looking for the stupid mortal who beat him. Probably with friends this time. Big, scaly friends who'd want nothing more than to tear you into little ‹race› pieces.\nI didn't scare you, did I...‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.1,"y":57.1,"n":"Tabetha","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"755":{"id":755,"t":"Rites of the Earthmother","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Seer Graytongue who lives in the hills directly south of Camp Narache.","desc":"Your willingness to perform a humble task for the tauren of Narache and your eagerness to learn are noble traits, ‹name›. I believe one day you will be heralded in Thunder Bluff as a ‹class› of greatness.\nBefore that you must embark on the Rites of the Earthmother, of which there are three.\nThe first test is the Rite of Strength. Travel to Seer Graytongue and tell him Chief Hawkwind has sent you.\nYou will find the seer's abode directly to the south of Camp Narache, tucked away in the hills.","rew":"Experience: 250\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Chief Hawkwind sent you? Embarking on the Rites of the Earthmother is no small task...","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":43.9,"y":76.7,"n":"Chief Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":42.5,"y":90.1,"n":"Seer Graytongue","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"98435":{"id":98435,"t":"Thunderhorns report","lv":10,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Thunderhorn's Report to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.\nCleanse the Wildmane Well","desc":"Our elders in Thunder Bluff must know of the progress we have made here, thanks to your aid.\nPlease, take this to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. You will find him in the Elder Rise, on the east side of the city. You must take the lifts up to the center of the city, then cross the bridges to reach it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCeremonial Tomahawk Dreamwatcher Staff\nExperience: 85\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Ah, no wonder there is such joy running through the streams of Mulgore. You have done a great service today. The wells provide much for not only our people, but to the wildlife we depend on for food, clothing, and companionship.\nIt is my humble pleasure to honor Mull's request. Please, accept this token of my gratitude.\nMulgore Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":48.4,"y":60.4,"n":"Mull Thunderhorn","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.4,"y":28.4,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9075":{"id":9075,"t":"Earthshatter Wristguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rimblat Earthshatter at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Earthshatter Wristguards if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Wristguards, 6 Wartorn Chain Scraps, 1 Arcanite Bar and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Wristguards Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Chain Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 14.4 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 13.5 % in Naxxramas , Spirit of Naxxramas 13.3 % in Naxxramas , Living Monstrosity 12.5 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcanite Bar\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Would you honor me by returning the armor of those that fell in the defense of these lands?\nThe armor has been desecrated and is undoubtedly being used for evil; however, with wartorn armor scraps, the desecrated armor can be renewed and worn for battle once more.\nBring me the remnants of the fallen along with purification materials and Earthshatter shall be yours to don.\nSearch Naxxramas.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarthshatter Wristguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Have you brought me that which I require?","done":"The wristguards are ready, ‹name›.\n<Rimblat bows.>","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":49.4,"n":"Rimblat Earthshatter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9235":{"id":9235,"t":"Icebane Bracers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -200g instead of 0.","obj":"Craftsman Wilhelm at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands wants 4 Frozen Runes, 12 Thorium Bars, 2 Arcanite Bars, 2 Essence of Water and 200 gold.\n4 Frozen Rune Frozen Rune in Naxxramas\n12 Thorium Bar\n2 Arcanite Bar\n2 Essence of Water Princess Tempestria 70.6 % , Lord Skwol 53.3 % , Hydrospawn 11 % , Toxic Horror 7.2 % and 4 more","desc":"Thanks to you and Omarion (May he rest in peace), I am now able to create Icebane bracers. All you need to do is bring me the materials and pay a small crafting fee.","rew":"You will receive:\nIcebane Bracers","back":"Have you brought the materials?","done":"Here is your order, ‹name›. Delivered as promised!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":49.9,"n":"Craftsman Wilhelm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"8915":{"id":8915,"t":"An Earnest Proposition","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -20g instead of 0.","obj":"Acquire 15 Silithus Venom Samples and 20 gold and bring them along with a set of Magister's Bindings to Mokvar in Orgrimmar.\n15 Silithus Venom Sample Stonelash Scorpid 30 % , Stonelash Pincer 30 % , Stonelash Flayer 30 % , Sand Skitterer 30 % and 1 more\nMagister's Bindings Rage Talon Fire Tongue 3.5 % , Firebrand Pyromancer 1.4 % , Scarshield Spellbinder 1.2 % , Bloodaxe Evoker 1.1 % and 1 more","desc":"Hail, ‹class›! I can tell by your demeanor that you've seen and done much in this world. Yet I'm willing to wager you haven't seen a piece of armor like this.\nPerform a small favor for me and I'll be willing to trade it to you for an ordinary set of bracers.\nI'm in need of a sizeable sample of venom drawn from the spiders and scorpions that inhabit Silithus. Bring this to me along with a few gold coins and I'll perform the exchange.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Bindings\nExperience: 6,600","back":"Have you obtained the items I require, ‹name›?","done":"Ah, yes. Mux will be quite happy with this.\nThose bindings were part of a larger armor set. If you're interested in providing me with further assistance, I'd be willing to consider parting with the rest of it.\nOrgrimmar Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"94435":{"id":94435,"t":"A lesson in divinity","lv":12,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep.","desc":"I don't know why you'd go out of your way to help me, but I appreciate it. If someone sent you my way, tell them I appreciate them too. You'll always have a friend in Tanis Alderwood, ‹class›.","rew":"You will receive:\nSymbol of Life\nExperience: 230","done":"You have done well, Gibari. It was a small thing, but even small acts of service such as this may help strengthen our connection to the light.\nThe Dark Lady and many in her service mistrust us. Some even conspire against us, but we will visit their skepticism and fear with courage and righteousness. We will show them that we are members of the Forsaken and we are willing to do our part, be it large or small, to help our people prosper once again.\nTake this symbol, you will need it for what comes next.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Tanis Alderwood","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":22,"y":44.6,"n":"Danitha Morr","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5635":{"id":5635,"t":"Desperate Prayer","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to High Priest Rohan in Ironforge.","desc":"You've caught the attention of our superiors, ‹name›. They've asked you travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priest Rohan. He will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.","rew":"You will learn: Desperate Prayer\nExperience: 210","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":47.3,"y":52.2,"n":"Maxan Anvol","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.5,"y":44.6,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"115":{"id":115,"t":"Shadow Magic","lv":23,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 30s instead of 15s.","obj":"Bring 3 Midnight Orbs to Marshal Marris in Lakeshire.\n3 Midnight Orb Blackrock Shadowcaster 80 %","desc":"The Blackrock orcs enlisted shadowcasters to aid their attacks in Redridge, and they have brought with them devices of dark power--midnight orbs. These orbs have struck telling blows against Redridge's defenders, and it's imperative we remove the demon-tainted items from the conflict.\nFind and deliver to me midnight orbs from slain Blackrock shadowcasters. I will then have them disposed of, for this world would be a better place without them!","rew":"Money: 30 0 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,300\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"How goes your conflict with the shadowcasters? Did you find the midnight orbs?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I'll send these to be destroyed immediately.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":28.4,"y":49,"n":"Marshal Marris","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"8835":{"id":8835,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Ironforge. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58,"y":28.6,"n":"Officer Ironbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"8355":{"id":8355,"t":"Incoming Gumdrop","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Do a train emote at Talvash del Kissel, and in exchange you'll receive a Gnomeregan Gumdrop!","desc":"A trick-or-treater! Huzzah!\nWell now, even though you're doing something noble and collecting candies for a sick child, I can't let you off the hook that easily. I have a yummy Gnomeregan Gumdrop to give to the sick child... if you make a train noise for me! Haha, yes, that'll be the trick! The price of this gumdrop is one train noise!\nChugga-chugga, ‹class›!","rew":"You will receive:\nGnomeregan Gumdrop","back":"Well, go ahead now...","done":"Too funny! Well done, ‹name›! Here's your treat.\nHappy Hallow's End!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.9,"y":21.7,"n":"Talvash del Kissel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"435":{"id":435,"t":"Escorting Erland","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Erland through the wolves, to Rane Yorick.","desc":"The wolves outside won't leave, and they eye me evilly every time I step foot out that door. They must be incredibly hungry to think I'm worth eating.\nI have to report to my teammate, the Deathstalker Rane Yorick. And to get to Rane, I'll need help against those wolves.\nPlease escort me! And there are a lot of wolves out there, so we'll have a better chance if you have friends who can help...","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathstalker Shortsword\nExperience: 875\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Please be brief. There is much danger about and we cannot stand idle in conversation.","done":"Thank you for the aid, ‹name›. I had feared Erland was overcome by the dangers of Silverpine. With your help, I see that he has not.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":56.2,"y":9.2,"n":"Deathstalker Erland","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":53.5,"y":13.4,"n":"Rane Yorick","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"81955":{"id":81955,"t":"A mind of metal","lv":45,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"A Mind of Metal","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 390","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nA Mind of Metal (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"915":{"id":915,"t":"You Scream, I Scream...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get some Strawberry Ice Cream for your ward. The lad seems to prefer Tigule and Foror's brand ice cream.\nTigule's Strawberry Ice Cream sold by Brivelthwerp , sold by Alowicious Czervik , sold by Emmithue Smails , sold by Katrina Shimmerstar and 1 more","desc":"ICE CREAM! Oh please please please could you get me some ice cream?! Strawberry is my favorite flavor, and there's no better strawberry ice cream in the world than Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream! It's my favorite ice cream in the whole wide world!\nI had it once a long time ago when I was at the Shimmering Flats race track, but I heard that they might be selling them in town now! Please? Pretty please? With Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream on top??!?!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Horde","back":"I wish they'd make more flavors of ice cream other than strawberry, but I guess I'm lucky that strawberry is my favorite!","done":"Mmmmmmmmm! I love their strawberry ice cream! If there's one thing Tigule and Foror know to do, it's make ice cream!\nThank you very much ‹name› - this is the best treat ever!\nStart Orcish Orphan End Orcish Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Horde Shareable No Quest ID 915\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 2,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] You Scream, I Scream... this quest\nGet some Strawberry Ice Cream for your ward.\nOrcish Orphan\n650 XP\n2 [ 60 ] A Warden of the Horde\nReturn your ward to the Orgrimmar orphanage by handing in the Orcish Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Battlewail in the Valley of Honor.\nOrcish Orphan\n1,650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1075":{"id":1075,"t":"A Scroll from Mauren","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Collin Mauren in Stormwind.","desc":"Okay, now for the remote detonation part of my plan... oh, I haven't explained that yet, have I?\nOkay, so the short of it is this: with a little magic, I can make it so the explosives go off while you're not around. I'm putting together a device that'll allow you to push just one button and have the NG-5 explode when you're ready.\nBut I need a spell from a friend in Stormwind--Collin Mauren is his name. You can find him in the mage quarter there. He's human, so he shouldn't be hard to miss.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Now, this spell you need; one that will allow you detonate explosives from a distance... hmmm.\nStonetalon Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59.5,"y":67.1,"n":"Gaxim Rustfizzle","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53,"y":86.6,"n":"Collin Mauren","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"7795":{"id":7795,"t":"A Donation of Runecloth","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, you've been a tremendous contributor to our cloth drive. As we work hard to replenish our reserves, one form of cloth remains critically low - runecloth. We are in absolutely dire need of runecloth, and we hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past.\nIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We'll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we'll go from there.","done":"Fantastic - these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We'd certainly be lost without you.\nWith all the donations you've made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I'll personally make sure that your good deeds won't go unrecognized!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":53.9,"y":81.7,"n":"Clavicus Knavingham","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"195":{"id":195,"t":"Raptor Mastery","lv":36,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Hemet Nesingwary wants you to kill 10 Lashtail Raptors.\nLashtail Raptor slain : 0/ 10","desc":"Now let's step up the challenge and see if you're up to it. Venture into the jungle and bag yourself 10 of those bloody Lashtail Raptors. Let's see what you've got!","rew":"Experience: 1,400","back":"A true hunter sets his focus on his prey. You, my friend, seem more concerned with chit-chatting around the campfire. Now get out there and kill 10 Lashtails before I go and rid the entire bloody jungle of them in one hunt.","done":"Now that's how you get a trophy or two over the ol' hearth! Nice killing, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"595":{"id":595,"t":"The Bloodsail Buccaneers","lv":41,"min":37,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"First Mate Crazz wants you to check the cove north of Booty Bay.","desc":"You sure seem eager to work, matey. Not sure why some land-loving ‹race› ‹class› is offering help to the Blackwater Raiders, but I'm not going to turn you away.\nOur ship just docked here in Booty Bay and word has it that our rivals--those damned, dirty Bloodsail Buccaneers--have been spotted all over southern Stranglethorn.\nAll the boys are too busy hitting the grog and looking for ladies! What I need is a scout.\nCheck the cove just north of Booty Bay along the Savage Coast and see what you find.","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,450\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Inside the skiff, you discover a map with some hastily written text on it along with some coins.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":28.1,"y":76.2,"n":"First Mate Crazz","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.3,"y":69.5,"n":"Bloodsail Correspondence","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8195":{"id":8195,"t":"Zulian, Razzashi, and Hakkari Coins","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Zulian Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nRazzashi Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nHakkari Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Some are sought after by my compatriots for various armors they offer Zandalar heroes. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Honor Token\nExperience: 650\n+25 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","done":"Excellent - this set of coins will make a fine addition to our growing collection... one that we will use in the tribe's defense against the rise of the Blood God. You've earned this Honor Token, ‹name›, as well as the thanks of the tribe!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.5,"y":15.8,"n":"Vinchaxa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"1475":{"id":1475,"t":"Into The Temple of Atal'Hakkar","lv":50,"min":38,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 38 instead of 41.","obj":"Gather 10 Atal'ai Tablets for Brohann Caskbelly in Stormwind.\n10 Atal'ai Tablet Atal'ai Tablet","desc":"According to legend, The Temple of Atal'Hakkar is a holy shrine dedicated to the ancient god, Hakkar the Soulflayer. Maintained by a vicious tribe of trolls named the Atal'ai, the temple is rumored to be impenetrable.\nNow sunk beneath the Pool of Tears, retrieving artifacts from the temple is even more difficult. But that's what I need you to do, ‹name›.\nAid me by gathering the intact Atal'ai Tablets. Bring them to me and I will return to the Explorers' Guild a hero. Together we will share the glory.","rew":"You will receive:\nGuardian Talisman\nExperience: 7,100\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"As dusk slowly descends upon my career I turn to you, ‹name›, to help me in my final quest for the Explorers' League. If my old bones could muster the strength to brave the Swamp of Sorrows and the sunken temple I would be fighting right alongside you.\nPride makes it hard for me to ask for your help in collecting the Atal'ai Tablets. But old age forces the necessity.\nPlease help me, ‹name›. I want to retire from the Explorers' League having completed their final bidding.","done":"The Atal'ai Tablets! Thank you, ‹name›!\nOnce I deliver these to the Explorers' League our names shall go down in history together. You have helped an old dwarf fulfill his final obligation in life. For that I am eternally grateful.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":69.5,"y":40.4,"n":"Brohann Caskbelly","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"8755":{"id":8755,"t":"The Path of the Conqueror","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight","rew":"You will receive:\nSignet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Dedication of this magnitude is a rarity. You have shown that your will is unfaltering, ‹name›. You shall be greatly rewarded for your stalwart watch over our world.\nHand me your signet ring so that I may strengthen its enchantment.","done":"Your rise amongst the rank of the Brood is most impressive, ‹name›. May you never stray from the path of the conqueror!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"355":{"id":355,"t":"Speak with Sevren","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Magistrate Sevren in Brill.","desc":"You have given me the remains of the Agamands, and satisfied my desire for revenge. But the Agamand Mills hold a threat to all the Forsaken, not just to me.\nI have spoken to Magistrate Sevren of your exploits against the Agamands, and he wishes to speak with you.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Coleman speaks well of you, ‹name›, telling of your successful forays into the Agamand Mills.\nThe Forsaken have need of your talents once again...","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.7,"y":52.3,"n":"Coleman Farthing","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2995":{"id":2995,"t":"Lines of Communication","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Oran Snakewrithe in Undercity wants you to travel to the Hinterlands and burn the Highvale Records, Highvale Report, and Highvale Notes.\nBurn the Highvale Records\nBurn the Highvale Notes\nBurn the Highvale Report","desc":"The Quel'Danil Lodge is a center of communication for the high elves of the Hinterlands. Their ambassadors are working to establish relationships with other races, with whom they share their knowledge of the Witherbark trolls that inhabit the area in the southern Hinterlands. All of the documents regarding the communications are kept at the lodge.\nWe don't need the Highvale building alliances with others, ‹name›.\nDestroy the Highvale documents. We need to burn their lines of communication... literally.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Keeping the Highvale elves isolated is the key. Have you found the lodge?","done":"Perfect, ‹name›. While the Highvale work to recover their lost information, we will be able to seal off the lines even further...\nUndercity The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":73.1,"y":32.8,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1715":{"id":1715,"t":"The Slaughtered Lamb","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.","desc":"Hmph. Times past, all warlocks in Khaz Modan were trained under the auspices of the masters of Gnomeregan, but now that we've all been forced to relocate into this rat's hole in Ironforge, and Magni's decided to keep a careful watch on us, we're forced to send our novices to Stormwind for training.\nLuckily, Gakin's no slouch, so you'll still learn what you need to know, but it burns my blood!\nAnyways, you'll find Gakin in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb in Stormwind.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Sent by Blackwrench, were you? Damn warlocks in Ironforge need to get things sorted out. There's only so much room and so many teachers in Stormwind. With all the increased traffic, we're sure to attract attention sooner or later.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.7,"y":22.6,"n":"Lago Blackwrench","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1795":{"id":1795,"t":"The Binding","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Using the Tome of the Cabal, summon and subdue a felhunter, then return the Tome of the Cabal to Strahad Farsan in Ratchet.\nTome of the Cabal\nSummoned Felhunter slain\nProvided: Tome of the Cabal","desc":"If you are sufficiently prepared, then we should begin. Let me explain the process to you.\nI will begin by creating the basic summoning circle. When that is finished, my acolytes will use the rods of channeling to create the greater circle.\nOnce that is done, read the incantation from the Tome of the Cabal, and the felhunter will be pulled forth. Be careful, ‹name›. A felhunter is a powerful foe, and I'd like to see you keep your head on your shoulders.","rew":"You will receive:\nBox of Souls\nYou will learn: Summon Felhunter\nExperience: 2,450","back":"Every warlock should have a felhunter at his command. Though it be difficult to tame, the powers it brings to its master far outweigh the cost.","done":"I must say I'm impressed, ‹name›. When I faced down my felhunter, I barely escaped with my life. I sense that you have the potential to become one of the most powerful warlocks of this era.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"7875":{"id":7875,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,900 experience instead of 5,500, 0.71 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 1 95 1 gold, 95 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,900\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The blood of our enemies is a mark of honor. Do you have such a mark?","done":"<Captain Shatterskull roars in triumph.>\nHow much more can they withstand? How many more Alliance filth must perish at the hands of the Horde for them to retreat? Only time will tell, ‹race›.\nLevel 45 , requires level 40 Difficulty 40 41 43 48 57 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7875","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"8435":{"id":8435,"t":"Battle of Warsong Gulch","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Marks of Honor to a Horde Warbringer outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The battle in Warsong Gulch against the Silverwing Sentinels is of great importance. Under the guise of protecting a forest that doesn't belong to them, the Alliance seeks to deny the Horde one of our largest sources for lumber.\nDo not let this happen, ‹name›! Come back to me with proof of serving the Horde in a worthy manner!","done":"Excellent! You've shown your worth by defending our operations in Warsong Gulch! May word of your honor spread far and wide across our lands.\nThe Barrens Arathi Highlands Undercity","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":46.7,"y":8.7,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.5,"y":29.1,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":58.3,"y":97.9,"n":"Horde Warbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5235":{"id":5235,"t":"Target: Gahrron's Withering","lv":58,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to Gahrron's Withering in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nGahrron's Withering Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Soulwrath\nEmpty Gahrron's Withering Bottle\nProvided: Empty Gahrron's Withering Bottle","desc":"The last cauldron that remains is located on a farm now called Gahrron's Withering. It is guarded by some of the Scourge's tougher minions - specifically, wraiths and ghosts. They are not to be trifled with, ‹name›.\nGahrron's Withering is far to the east of the Bulwark, close to where the Eastern Plaguelands begin; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key. Here is your empty sample bottle; bring it to me filled. May the shadows cloak you in safety for this dangerous mission, ‹class›.","rew":"Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"Cauldron Lord Soulwrath's key disintegrates as it touches the lock on the access panel at the base of the cauldron's platform. A slight clanking noise is heard within, and the access panel swings open to reveal more viscous toxins within the cauldron's framework.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for Shadow Priestess Vandis back at the Bulwark.\nTirisfal Glades Western Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83,"y":71.9,"n":"Shadow Priestess Vandis","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":62.5,"y":58.5,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"275":{"id":275,"t":"Blisters on The Land","lv":26,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Blisters on The Land.","obj":"Kill 8 Fen Creepers, then return to Rethiel the Greenwarden in the Wetlands.\nFen Creeper slain : 0/ 8","desc":"I do not know why, but a festering grows within the Wetlands. Fen Creepers have risen. They are diseased, fevered blisters on the land, and for the fever to break they must be dispatched and allowed to settle back into the marshes.\nThe Fen Creepers shamble amidst the waterways of the Wetlands.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFen Keeper Robe Forest Chain Phytoblade\nExperience: 2,650","back":"The Wetlands still weep, and the Fen Creepers still rage. Return to me when your task is done.","done":"This land is soothed by your efforts, and for this I will grant you a boon.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":56.4,"y":40.4,"n":"Rethiel the Greenwarden","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92515":{"id":92515,"t":"The problem with prideclaws","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Prideclaw Pelts from the Prideclaws in Shen'dar Highlands.\n10 Prideclaw Pelt","desc":"As if bandits and mad cultists weren't enough, the hills are thick with prideclaws as well right now. They are starting to encroach on the village borders and growing bolder by the day. It's only a matter of time before someone's pet or child is taken. It would be a mercy for us to cull their numbers now rather than after some tragedy occurs.\nBring me a dozen or so of their pelts. I can turn them into all sorts of goods that will be of aid to the village.","rew":"You will receive:\nSimple Leather Satchel\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","back":"If you ask me, I think Prideclaws are actually kind of cute. From a safe distance... and while standing behind someone holding a sword, of course.","done":"I didn't say it wouldn't be a dirty job, did I?","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.6,"y":44.4,"n":"Indari Sunseam","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"92595":{"id":92595,"t":"The windshapers","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Listen to what Illaya Amberwind has to say.\nListen to Illaya","desc":"<Illaya smiles warmly at you.>\nI am glad you returned to speak with me, child of the winds. I knew it the first moment you walked into my presence, that you were strong in the skysight. Do you find this surprising? Even those who have not trained as a Shaman may possess the gift.\nCome, let us speak about the mandate of the Windshapers, the nature of our struggles on Zephras, and the plight of our people.","back":"The world is changing and the path forward will be difficult. We have but one chance to save ourselves.","done":"I think you now understand how important the mission of the Windshapers is. Every soul who commands the skysight is of vital importance if we hope to establish dialogue with the spirits of the winds once again.\nBetween threats from within such as the Al'Aketh, and the uncertainty of our safety here in Skywall, it is our responsibility as Windshapers to use our gifts to save our home and ensure that the Shen'dorei can survive these trying times.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":43.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Illaya Amberwind","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});